description: "Which scale degrees sound stable or unstable, where their tendencies lead, and how to use this hierarchy in melody, improvisation, and analysis."
keywords: "stable and unstable notes, stable scale degrees, unstable scale degrees, tendency tones, note resolution, scale degrees, melody"
categories: "Keys, Melody"
tags: "stability, instability, scale degrees, melody, tendency tones"
date: 2026-08-02
intro: "Within one key, a note can sound like a full stop while another feels like an unfinished sentence. The difference does not come from pitch alone, but from the note’s relationship to the tonic, the current chord, and its position in the phrase."
reader_level: arranger
